     "text": "Roman Moreno and Turner Clinic\nRe: Barbara Holland (DOB 12/11/1982)\n\nApril 17, 2025: Ms. Holland was seen today for her annual physical. Her blood pressure was 121/77 and her weight was 134 pounds. Upon review of her medical history, it is noted that she has a known Stroke (CVA) that occurred 13.2 years ago on February 27, 2012. She remains on aspirin 81 mg to help manage her condition. Her neurological exam was within normal limits, and she reported no recent episodes of dizziness or other concerning symptoms. She has also been following a healthy diet and engaging in light exercise, as tolerated.\n\nDecember 03, 2024: Ms. Holland visited today regarding her Stroke (CVA). Her blood pressure was 119/70 and her weight was 136 pounds. She continues to do well with no recurrent events. She is adherent to her medication regimen which includes aspirin 81 mg. A routine neurological examination showed no acute deficits.\n\nJuly 20, 2024: Ms. Holland was seen today for a follow-up regarding her Stroke (CVA). Her blood pressure was 120/76 and her weight was 140 pounds. She is doing well with no new complaints. Aspirin 81 mg is being continued for stroke prevention. Her neurological exam was unremarkable, and she reported no recent transient ischemic attacks or other neurological symptoms.\n\nMarch 06, 2024: Ms. Holland was seen today for evaluation of a rash. Her blood pressure was 129/79\n"
