     "page": 1,
     "text": "Page 2  -- ROI --\nMunoz Inc Medical Group\nRe: Barbara Holland (DOB 12/11/1982)\n\nApril 11, 2025: Ms. Barbara Holland visited today for routine follow-up regarding Psoriasis and psoriatic arthritis. During this visit, her blood pressure was recorded at 130/74, and weight was 131 pounds. Ms. Holland reports that she is feeling well overall, with her psoriasis symptoms under control. She continues on her biologic therapy without any issues or side effects. She also mentioned a minor, unrelated complaint of occasional dry eyes, which we addressed with reassurance and advised the use of lubricating eye drops as needed.\n\nSeptember 26, 2024: Ms. Holland was seen on this date for ongoing management of Psoriasis and psoriatic arthritis. Her blood pressure was 126/72, and her weight was 127 pounds. The patient continues to do well on her biologic therapy. There are no new complaints, and her arthritis remains controlled. She has also reported occasional headaches, which we believe are unrelated to her primary condition. She was advised to continue her current regimen and monitor her symptoms.\n\nMarch 12, 2024: Ms. Holland was seen for her Psoriasis and psoriatic arthritis on this date. Her blood pressure was 129/78, and her weight was 134 pounds. She is doing well overall. She reports that her psoriasis symptoms are well-controlled with her current biologic therapy. She has no new complaints. Additionally, she mentioned mild which we discussed as possibly related to her overall health and lifestyle factors. She continues on her current medication regimen.\n\nAugust 27, 2023: Ms. Holland visited for her Psoriasis and psoriatic arthritis. Her blood pressure was 132/67, and her weight was 139 pounds. She continues on biologic therapy with good control of her arthritis symptoms. She reports no new issues or complications. There were no changes to her treatment plan. During this visit, she also mentioned occasional muscle stiffness, which we discussed as potentially related to her psoriatic arthritis or general musculoskeletal health. \n\nSocial History: Ms. Holland uses tobacco in the form of cigars, with a frequency of approximately five times per year. She started this habit on May 29, 2022, and has not quit. Additionally, she consumes alcohol with an average of about 10 drinks per week. Her responses suggest she has minimized the disclosure of her tobacco use.\n\nSincerely,\n\nDr. Matthew Inc Medical Group\n"
